# Git branches (Silvervibe)

## Long-lived

- **`main`** — production / public landing on silvervibe.io. Do not push unfinished work.
- **`develop`** — integration branch. Do not commit issue work directly here.

## Issue branches (required)

For every GitHub issue, cut a branch from up-to-date `develop`:

```text
{type}/{number}-{short-kebab-slug}
```

| Type | When |
| --- | --- |
| `feature/` | New capability, foundation, enhancements |
| `bugfix/` | Defects |
| `docs/` | Docs-only |
| `chore/` | CI, tooling, repo process |

Examples: `feature/3-neon-postgres`, `docs/1-local-dev-environment`, `bugfix/12-info-email-routing`.

```bash
git checkout develop && git pull origin develop
git checkout -b feature/<n>-<slug>
# PR base = develop; body closes #<n>
```

## Landing

- Do not change the silvervibe landing page unless the user explicitly asks to ship a landing update (then PR → `develop`, promote to `main` when ready).
- New routes: issue branch → `develop`; do not link from the public landing until ready. Keep unknown paths redirecting home.

See `docs/branching.md`.
